#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "GIT bitmap v1 format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pack and multi-pack bitmaps"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:9
msgid ""
"Bitmaps store reachability information about the set of objects in a "
"packfile, or a multi-pack index (MIDX). The former is defined obviously, and "
"the latter is defined as the union of objects in packs contained in the "
"MIDX."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:12
msgid ""
"A bitmap may belong to either one pack, or the repository's multi-pack index "
"(if it exists). A repository may have at most one bitmap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:14
msgid "An object is uniquely described by its bit position within a bitmap:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:19
msgid ""
"If the bitmap belongs to a packfile, the __n__th bit corresponds to the "
"__n__th object in pack order. For a function `offset` which maps objects to "
"their byte offset within a pack, pack order is defined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:21
#, no-wrap
msgid "o1 <= o2 <==> offset(o1) <= offset(o2)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:26
msgid ""
"If the bitmap belongs to a MIDX, the __n__th bit corresponds to the __n__th "
"object in MIDX order. With an additional function `pack` which maps objects "
"to the pack they were selected from by the MIDX, MIDX order is defined as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "o1 <= o2 <==> pack(o1) <= pack(o2) /\\ offset(o1) <= offset(o2)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:31
msgid ""
"The ordering between packs is done according to the MIDX's .rev file.  "
"Notably, the preferred pack sorts ahead of all other packs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:35
msgid ""
"The on-disk representation (described below) of a bitmap is the same "
"regardless of whether or not that bitmap belongs to a packfile or a "
"MIDX. The only difference is the interpretation of the bits, which is "
"described above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:39
msgid ""
"Certain bitmap extensions are supported (see: Appendix B). No extensions are "
"required for bitmaps corresponding to packfiles. For bitmaps that correspond "
"to MIDXs, both the bit-cache and rev-cache extensions are required."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "On-disk format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:43
msgid "A header appears at the beginning:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "4-byte signature: "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:45
msgid "{'B', 'I', 'T', 'M'}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "2-byte version number (network byte order): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The current implementation only supports version 1\n"
"of the bitmap index (the same one as JGit).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "2-byte flags (network byte order): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following flags are supported:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:56
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:68
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:76
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:121
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:127
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:145
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:153
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:242
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:247
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:251
msgid "{empty}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "BITMAP_OPT_FULL_DAG (0x1) REQUIRED: "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:66
msgid ""
"This flag must always be present. It implies that the bitmap index has been "
"generated for a packfile or multi-pack index (MIDX) with full closure "
"(i.e. where every single object in the packfile/MIDX can find its parent "
"links inside the same packfile/MIDX). This is a requirement for the bitmap "
"index format, also present in JGit, that greatly reduces the complexity of "
"the implementation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "BITMAP_OPT_HASH_CACHE (0x4): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:74
msgid ""
"If present, the end of the bitmap file contains `N` 32-bit name-hash values, "
"one per object in the pack/MIDX. The format and meaning of the name-hash is "
"described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "BITMAP_OPT_LOOKUP_TABLE (0x10): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:81
msgid ""
"If present, the end of the bitmap file contains a table containing a list of "
"`N` <commit_pos, offset, xor_row> triplets. The format and meaning of the "
"table is described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:85
msgid ""
"Unlike the xor_offset used to compress an individual bitmap, `xor_row` "
"stores an *absolute* index into the lookup table, not a location relative to "
"the current entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "4-byte entry count (network byte order): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "The total count of entries (bitmapped commits) in this bitmap index.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "20-byte checksum: "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The SHA1 checksum of the pack/MIDX this bitmap index\n"
"belongs to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:94
msgid "4 EWAH bitmaps that act as type indexes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:98
msgid ""
"Type indexes are serialized after the hash cache in the shape of four EWAH "
"bitmaps stored consecutively (see Appendix A for the serialization format of "
"an EWAH bitmap)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:101
msgid "There is a bitmap for each Git object type, stored in the following order:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:103
msgid "Commits"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:104
msgid "Trees"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:105
msgid "Blobs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:106
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:110
msgid ""
"In each bitmap, the `n`th bit is set to true if the `n`th object in the "
"packfile or multi-pack index is of that type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:114
msgid ""
"The obvious consequence is that the OR of all 4 bitmaps will result in a "
"full set (all bits set), and the AND of all 4 bitmaps will result in an "
"empty bitmap (no bits set)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:116
msgid "N entries with compressed bitmaps, one for each indexed commit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:119
msgid ""
"Where `N` is the total number of entries in this bitmap index.  Each entry "
"contains the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "4-byte object position (network byte order): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The position **in the index for the packfile or\n"
"multi-pack index** where the bitmap for this commit is\n"
"found.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:127
#, no-wrap
msgid "1-byte XOR-offset: "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:133
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The xor offset used to compress this bitmap. For an entry\n"
"in position `x`, an XOR offset of `y` means that the actual\n"
"bitmap representing this commit is composed by XORing the\n"
"bitmap for this entry with the bitmap in entry `x-y` (i.e.\n"
"the bitmap `y` entries before this one).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:137
msgid ""
"This compression can be recursive. In order to XOR this entry with a "
"previous one, the previous entry needs to be decompressed first, and so on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:143
msgid ""
"The hard-limit for this offset is 160 (an entry can only be xor'ed against "
"one of the 160 entries preceding it). This number is always positive, and "
"hence entries are always xor'ed with **previous** bitmaps, not bitmaps that "
"will come afterwards in the index."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:145
#, no-wrap
msgid "1-byte flags for this bitmap: "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:149
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the moment the only available flag is `0x1`, which hints\n"
"that this bitmap can be re-used when rebuilding bitmap indexes\n"
"for the repository.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:151
msgid "The compressed bitmap itself, see Appendix A."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:153
#, no-wrap
msgid "TRAILER: "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trailing checksum of the preceding contents.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:156
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix A: Serialization format for an EWAH bitmap"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:161
msgid ""
"Ewah bitmaps are serialized in the same protocol as the JAVAEWAH library, "
"making them backwards compatible with the JGit implementation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:163
msgid "4-byte number of bits of the resulting UNCOMPRESSED bitmap"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:165
msgid "4-byte number of words of the COMPRESSED bitmap, when stored"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:167
msgid "N x 8-byte words, as specified by the previous field"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:169
msgid "This is the actual content of the compressed bitmap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:171
msgid "4-byte position of the current RLW for the compressed bitmap"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:174
msgid "All words are stored in network byte order for their corresponding sizes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:178
msgid ""
"The compressed bitmap is stored in a form of run-length encoding, as "
"follows.  It consists of a concatenation of an arbitrary number of chunks.  "
"Each chunk consists of one or more 64-bit words"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "     H  L_1  L_2  L_3 .... L_M\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:183
msgid ""
"H is called RLW (run length word).  It consists of (from lower to higher "
"order bits):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:185
msgid "1 bit: the repeated bit B"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:186
msgid "32 bits: repetition count K (unsigned)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:187
msgid "31 bits: literal word count M (unsigned)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:189
msgid "The bitstream represented by the above chunk is then:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:191
msgid "K repetitions of B"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:194
msgid ""
"The bits stored in `L_1` through `L_M`.  Within a word, bits at lower order "
"come earlier in the stream than those at higher order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:198
msgid ""
"The next word after `L_M` (if any) must again be a RLW, for the next chunk.  "
"For efficient appending to the bitstream, the EWAH stores a pointer to the "
"last RLW in the stream."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix B: Optional Bitmap Sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:204
msgid ""
"These sections may or may not be present in the `.bitmap` file; their "
"presence is indicated by the header flags section described above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:206
#, no-wrap
msgid "Name-hash cache"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:214
msgid ""
"If the BITMAP_OPT_HASH_CACHE flag is set, the end of the bitmap contains a "
"cache of 32-bit values, one per object in the pack/MIDX. The value at "
"position `i` is the hash of the pathname at which the `i`th object (counting "
"in index or multi-pack index order) in the pack/MIDX can be found.  This can "
"be fed into the delta heuristics to compare objects with similar pathnames."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:216
msgid "The hash algorithm used is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:221
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    hash = 0;\n"
"    while ((c = *name++))\n"
"\t    if (!isspace(c))\n"
"\t\t    hash = (hash >> 2) + (c << 24);\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:226
msgid ""
"Note that this hashing scheme is tied to the BITMAP_OPT_HASH_CACHE flag.  If "
"implementations want to choose a different hashing scheme, they are free to "
"do so, but MUST allocate a new header flag (because comparing hashes made "
"under two different schemes would be pointless)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:228
#, no-wrap
msgid "Commit lookup table"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:235
msgid ""
"If the BITMAP_OPT_LOOKUP_TABLE flag is set, the last `N * (4 + 8 + 4)` bytes "
"(preceding the name-hash cache and trailing hash) of the `.bitmap` file "
"contains a lookup table specifying the information needed to get the desired "
"bitmap from the entries without parsing previous unnecessary bitmaps."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:240
msgid ""
"For a `.bitmap` containing `nr_entries` reachability bitmaps, the table "
"contains a list of `nr_entries` <commit_pos, offset, xor_row> triplets "
"(sorted in the ascending order of `commit_pos`). The content of the i'th "
"triplet is -"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:242
#, no-wrap
msgid "commit_pos (4 byte integer, network byte order): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:245
msgid "It stores the object position of a commit (in the midx or pack index)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:247
#, no-wrap
msgid "offset (8 byte integer, network byte order): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:249
msgid "The offset from which that commit's bitmap can be read."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:251
#, no-wrap
msgid "xor_row (4 byte integer, network byte order): "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:254
msgid ""
"The position of the triplet whose bitmap is used to compress this one, or "
"`0xffffffff` if no such bitmap exists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:256
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pseudo-merge bitmaps"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:261
msgid ""
"If the `BITMAP_OPT_PSEUDO_MERGES` flag is set, a variable number of bytes "
"(preceding the name-hash cache, commit lookup table, and trailing checksum) "
"of the `.bitmap` file is used to store pseudo-merge bitmaps."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:264
msgid ""
"For more information on what pseudo-merges are, why they are useful, and how "
"to configure them, see the information in linkgit:gitpacking[7]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:265
#, no-wrap
msgid "File format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:269
msgid ""
"If enabled, pseudo-merge bitmaps are stored in an optional section at the "
"end of a `.bitmap` file. The format is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block .
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:332
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"+-------------------------------------------+\n"
"|               .bitmap File                |\n"
"+-------------------------------------------+\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  Pseudo-merge bitmaps (Variable Length)   |\n"
"|  +---------------------------+            |\n"
"|  | commits_bitmap (EWAH)     |            |\n"
"|  +---------------------------+            |\n"
"|  | merge_bitmap (EWAH)       |            |\n"
"|  +---------------------------+            |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"+-------------------------------------------+\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  Lookup Table                             |\n"
"|  +---------------------------+            |\n"
"|  | commit_pos (4 bytes)      |            |\n"
"|  +---------------------------+            |\n"
"|  | offset (8 bytes)          |            |\n"
"|  +------------+--------------+            |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  Offset Cases:                            |\n"
"|  -------------                            |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  1. MSB Unset: single pseudo-merge bitmap |\n"
"|     + offset to pseudo-merge bitmap       |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  2. MSB Set: multiple pseudo-merges       |\n"
"|     + offset to extended lookup table     |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"+-------------------------------------------+\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  Extended Lookup Table (Optional)         |\n"
"|  +----+----------+----------+----------+  |\n"
"|  | N  | Offset 1 |   ....   | Offset N |  |\n"
"|  +----+----------+----------+----------+  |\n"
"|  |    |  8 bytes |   ....   |  8 bytes |  |\n"
"|  +----+----------+----------+----------+  |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"+-------------------------------------------+\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  Pseudo-merge position table              |\n"
"|  +----+----------+----------+----------+  |\n"
"|  | N  | Offset 1 |   ....   | Offset N |  |\n"
"|  +----+----------+----------+----------+  |\n"
"|  |    |  8 bytes |   ....   |  8 bytes |  |\n"
"|  +----+----------+----------+----------+  |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"+-------------------------------------------+\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"|  Pseudo-merge Metadata                    |\n"
"|  +-----------------------------------+    |\n"
"|  | # pseudo-merges (4 bytes)         |    |\n"
"|  +-----------------------------------+    |\n"
"|  | # commits (4 bytes)               |    |\n"
"|  +-----------------------------------+    |\n"
"|  | Lookup offset (8 bytes)           |    |\n"
"|  +-----------------------------------+    |\n"
"|  | Extension size (8 bytes)          |    |\n"
"|  +-----------------------------------+    |\n"
"|                                           |\n"
"+-------------------------------------------+\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:335
msgid "One or more pseudo-merge bitmaps, each containing:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:338
msgid ""
"`commits_bitmap`, an EWAH-compressed bitmap describing the set of commits "
"included in the this psuedo-merge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:342
msgid ""
"`merge_bitmap`, an EWAH-compressed bitmap describing the union of the set of "
"objects reachable from all commits listed in the `commits_bitmap`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:347
msgid ""
"A lookup table, mapping pseudo-merged commits to the pseudo-merges they "
"belong to. Entries appear in increasing order of each commit's bit "
"position. Each entry is 12 bytes wide, and is comprised of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:350
msgid ""
"`commit_pos`, a 4-byte unsigned value (in network byte-order)  containing "
"the bit position for this commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:352
msgid "`offset`, an 8-byte unsigned value (also in network byte-order)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:354
msgid ""
"containing either one of two possible offsets, depending on whether or not "
"the most-significant bit is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:356
msgid "If unset (i.e. `offset & ((uint64_t)1<<63) == 0`), the offset"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:359
msgid ""
"(relative to the beginning of the `.bitmap` file) at which the pseudo-merge "
"bitmap for this commit can be read. This indicates only a single "
"pseudo-merge bitmap contains this commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:361
msgid "If set (i.e. `offset & ((uint64_t)1<<63) != 0`), the offset"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:365
msgid ""
"(again relative to the beginning of the `.bitmap` file) at which the "
"extended offset table can be located describing the set of pseudo-merge "
"bitmaps which contain this commit. This indicates that multiple pseudo-merge "
"bitmaps contain this commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:370
msgid ""
"An (optional) extended lookup table (written if and only if there is at "
"least one commit which appears in more than one pseudo-merge).  There are as "
"many entries as commits which appear in multiple pseudo-merges. Each entry "
"contains the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:373
msgid ""
"`N`, a 4-byte unsigned value equal to the number of pseudo-merges which "
"contain a given commit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:378
msgid ""
"An array of `N` 8-byte unsigned values, each of which is interpreted as an "
"offset (relative to the beginning of the `.bitmap` file) at which a "
"pseudo-merge bitmap for this commit can be read. These values occur in no "
"particular order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:382
msgid ""
"Positions for all pseudo-merges, each stored as an 8-byte unsigned value (in "
"network byte-order) containing the offset (relative to the beginning of the "
"`.bitmap` file) of each consecutive pseudo-merge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:385
msgid ""
"A 4-byte unsigned value (in network byte-order) equal to the number of "
"pseudo-merges."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:388
msgid ""
"A 4-byte unsigned value (in network byte-order) equal to the number of "
"unique commits which appear in any pseudo-merge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:392
msgid ""
"An 8-byte unsigned value (in network byte-order) equal to the number of "
"bytes between the start of the pseudo-merge section and the beginning of the "
"lookup table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/bitmap-format.txt:394
msgid ""
"An 8-byte unsigned value (in network byte-order) equal to the number of "
"bytes in the pseudo-merge section (including this field)."
msgstr ""
